-- The 2023 Merger Guidelines, section 2.1 (Guideline 1): concentration, the HHI and the structural presumption.
-- AGENCY ENFORCEMENT POLICY, NOT LAW: the presumption is the Agencies' ("the Agencies therefore presume, unless
-- sufficiently disproved or rebutted", section 1, [pdf page 3 of 51]); it is not a holding that a merger is unlawful.
--
-- Two layers. The arithmetic (the HHI, the change in it, the threshold predicates) is total on numbers, impossible ones
-- included, and is exactly what the text says. The results a reader asks for on given metrics (the two limbs, the
-- presumption on the metrics, footnote 15's band) answer NOTHING when a metric is impossible: an HHI outside 0 to 10,000,
-- a change below 0 or above the post-merger HHI, a share outside 0 to 100. They do not check that the metrics could come
-- from one market together (a merged share of 10 cannot produce a change of 101): only the market reading computes them. `the Agencies' reading under Guideline 1 of` takes a market, checks that it is one the
-- text can read (fork G1-2 in NOTES.md), and answers NOTHING when it is not.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mg-nouns`

§ `2.1 Guideline 1: Mergers Raise a Presumption of Illegality When They Significantly Increase Concentration in a Highly Concentrated Market`

§§ `2.1 the HHI`

-- [pdf page 6 of 51]: "The HHI is defined as the sum of the squares of the market shares"; "reaching 10,000 in a market
-- with a single firm".
@ref Merger Guidelines 2023, section 2.1 [pdf page 6 of 51]
GIVEN shares IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the HHI of the shares` MEANS sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD s TIMES s) shares)

-- Footnote 14, [pdf page 7 of 51]: "The change in HHI from a merger of firms with shares a and b is equal to 2ab."
@ref Merger Guidelines 2023, section 2.1, footnote 14 [pdf page 7 of 51]
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the change in HHI from merging firms with shares` MEANS 2 TIMES a TIMES b

-- The pre-merger shares of the market, and the post-merger shares, with the parties' shares added together into one
-- firm's (fork G1-1: the merged firm's share is the sum of the parties' pre-merger shares; that is what makes footnote
-- 14's 2ab the change).
GIVEN market IS A LIST OF `Firm in the relevant market`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the pre-merger shares of` MEANS map (GIVEN f YIELD f's `the firm's pre-merger share`) market

GIVEN market IS A LIST OF `Firm in the relevant market`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the merged firm's share in` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN f YIELD f's `the firm's pre-merger share`)
             (filter (GIVEN f YIELD f's `the firm is a party to the merger`) market))

GIVEN market IS A LIST OF `Firm in the relevant market`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the post-merger shares of` MEANS
    `the merged firm's share in` market
        FOLLOWED BY map (GIVEN f YIELD f's `the firm's pre-merger share`)
                        (filter (GIVEN f YIELD NOT (f's `the firm is a party to the merger`)) market)

GIVEN market IS A LIST OF `Firm in the relevant market`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pre-merger HHI of` MEANS `the HHI of the shares` (`the pre-merger shares of` market)

GIVEN market IS A LIST OF `Firm in the relevant market`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the post-merger HHI of` MEANS `the HHI of the shares` (`the post-merger shares of` market)

GIVEN market IS A LIST OF `Firm in the relevant market`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the change in HHI of` MEANS `the post-merger HHI of` market MINUS `the pre-merger HHI of` market

§§ `2.1 the thresholds`

-- [pdf page 6 of 51]: "Markets with an HHI greater than 1,800 are highly concentrated, and a change of more than 100
-- points is a significant increase."
@ref Merger Guidelines 2023, section 2.1 [pdf page 6 of 51]
GIVEN hhi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `highly concentrated, by an HHI of` IF hhi GREATER THAN 1800

@ref Merger Guidelines 2023, section 2.1 [pdf page 6 of 51]
GIVEN change IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a significant increase, by a change in HHI of` IF change GREATER THAN 100

-- [pdf page 7 of 51]: "a merger that creates a firm with a share over thirty percent".
@ref Merger Guidelines 2023, section 2.1 [pdf page 7 of 51]
GIVEN share IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a merged firm's share over thirty percent, by a share of` IF share GREATER THAN 30

-- The table "Indicator Threshold for Structural Presumption", [pdf page 7 of 51]: Market HHI, Post-merger HHI greater
-- than 1,800 AND Change in HHI greater than 100; or Merged Firm's Market Share, Share greater than 30% AND Change in HHI
-- greater than 100. "Creates or further consolidates a highly concentrated market" ([pdf page 6 of 51], and the
-- overview at [pdf page 3 of 51]) is read as the table's post-merger HHI over 1,800 (fork G1-3).
-- The impossible metrics. Each HHI is on 0 to 10,000; the change is post-merger HHI minus pre-merger HHI, and the
-- pre-merger HHI is not negative, so the change is at most the post-merger HHI; a merger does not lower the HHI, so the
-- change is not negative (fork G1-1: the change is 2(ab + bc + ...) of the parties' shares).
GIVEN hhi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an HHI is impossible` IF hhi LESS THAN 0 OR hhi GREATER THAN 10000

GIVEN `post HHI` IS A NUMBER
      `HHI change` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a post-merger HHI and its change are impossible` IF
       `an HHI is impossible` `post HHI`
    OR `HHI change` LESS THAN 0
    OR `HHI change` GREATER THAN `post HHI`

GIVEN share IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a share is impossible` IF share LESS THAN 0 OR share GREATER THAN 100

@ref Merger Guidelines 2023, section 2.1, table [pdf page 7 of 51]
GIVEN `post HHI` IS A NUMBER
      `HHI change` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the HHI limb of the presumption is met by` MEANS
    IF `a post-merger HHI and its change are impossible` `post HHI` `HHI change`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`highly concentrated, by an HHI of` `post HHI` AND `a significant increase, by a change in HHI of` `HHI change`)

@ref Merger Guidelines 2023, section 2.1, table [pdf page 7 of 51]
GIVEN `merged share` IS A NUMBER
      `HHI change` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the share limb of the presumption is met by` MEANS
    IF `a share is impossible` `merged share` OR `HHI change` LESS THAN 0 OR `HHI change` GREATER THAN 10000
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`a merged firm's share over thirty percent, by a share of` `merged share` AND `a significant increase, by a change in HHI of` `HHI change`)

-- The table's "or": either limb raises the presumption.
@ref Merger Guidelines 2023, section 2.1, table [pdf page 7 of 51]
GIVEN `the HHI limb is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share limb is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Guideline 1 presumption`
`the Guideline 1 presumption, given its two limbs` MEANS
    IF `the HHI limb is met` OR `the share limb is met`
    THEN `the Agencies presume the merger may substantially lessen competition, unless sufficiently disproved or rebutted`
    ELSE `no structural presumption arises under Guideline 1, and the other Guidelines may still apply`

@ref Merger Guidelines 2023, section 2.1, table [pdf page 7 of 51]
GIVEN `post HHI` IS A NUMBER
      `HHI change` IS A NUMBER
      `merged share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Guideline 1 presumption`
`the Guideline 1 presumption on the metrics` MEANS
    IF `a post-merger HHI and its change are impossible` `post HHI` `HHI change` OR `a share is impossible` `merged share`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the Guideline 1 presumption, given its two limbs`
                   (`highly concentrated, by an HHI of` `post HHI` AND `a significant increase, by a change in HHI of` `HHI change`)
                   (`a merged firm's share over thirty percent, by a share of` `merged share` AND `a significant increase, by a change in HHI of` `HHI change`))

§§ `2.1 a market the text can read`

-- Fork G1-2: every firm in the relevant market is listed (the fringe too, each with its own share), no share is
-- negative or over 100, the shares add up to exactly 100, and at least one firm is a party to the merger. Otherwise the
-- answer is NOTHING: the text gives no HHI for a market whose shares are not all known.
GIVEN market IS A LIST OF `Firm in the relevant market`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the market is one Guideline 1 can read` IF
        all (GIVEN f YIELD f's `the firm's pre-merger share` AT LEAST 0) market
    AND all (GIVEN f YIELD f's `the firm's pre-merger share` AT MOST 100) market
    AND sum (`the pre-merger shares of` market) EQUALS 100
    AND any (GIVEN f YIELD f's `the firm is a party to the merger`) market

@ref Merger Guidelines 2023, section 2.1 [pdf pages 6 and 7 of 51]
GIVEN market IS A LIST OF `Firm in the relevant market`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Guideline 1 finding`
`the Agencies' reading under Guideline 1 of` MEANS
    IF `the market is one Guideline 1 can read` market
    THEN JUST (`Guideline 1 finding` WITH
                  `pre-merger HHI` IS `the pre-merger HHI of` market
                  `post-merger HHI` IS `the post-merger HHI of` market
                  `change in HHI` IS `the change in HHI of` market
                  `merged firm's share` IS `the merged firm's share in` market
                  `highly concentrated after the merger` IS `highly concentrated, by an HHI of` (`the post-merger HHI of` market)
                  `significant increase in concentration` IS `a significant increase, by a change in HHI of` (`the change in HHI of` market)
                  `merged firm's share over thirty percent` IS `a merged firm's share over thirty percent, by a share of` (`the merged firm's share in` market)
                  `the HHI limb is met` IS `HHI limb`
                  `the share limb is met` IS `share limb`
                  `the presumption` IS `the Guideline 1 presumption, given its two limbs` `HHI limb` `share limb`)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `HHI limb` MEANS     `highly concentrated, by an HHI of` (`the post-merger HHI of` market)
                         AND `a significant increase, by a change in HHI of` (`the change in HHI of` market)
        `share limb` MEANS     `a merged firm's share over thirty percent, by a share of` (`the merged firm's share in` market)
                           AND `a significant increase, by a change in HHI of` (`the change in HHI of` market)

-- "The higher the concentration metrics over these thresholds, ... the stronger the evidence needed to rebut or
-- disprove it" ([pdf page 7 of 51]): the finding reports the three metrics, so a reader sees how far over the
-- thresholds they are. The text gives no scale for the evidence, so nothing here weighs it.

§§ `2.1 footnotes 15 and 21: the bands`

-- Footnote 15 ([pdf page 7 of 51]) records the 1982 bands (above 1,000 "concentrated", 1,000 to 1,800 "moderately
-- concentrated", above 1,800 "highly concentrated") and says the Agencies "have therefore returned to those thresholds";
-- footnote 21 ([pdf page 11 of 51]): "A concentrated market is one with an HHI greater than 1,000 (See Guideline 1, n.15)."
@ref Merger Guidelines 2023, section 2.4, footnote 21 [pdf page 11 of 51]
GIVEN hhi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `concentrated, by an HHI of` IF hhi GREATER THAN 1000

@ref Merger Guidelines 2023, footnotes 15 and 21 [pdf pages 7 and 11 of 51]
GIVEN hhi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Concentration band`
`the concentration band of an HHI of` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an HHI is impossible` hhi                THEN NOTHING
        IF `highly concentrated, by an HHI of` hhi THEN JUST `highly concentrated (HHI greater than 1,800)`
        IF `concentrated, by an HHI of` hhi        THEN JUST `concentrated but not highly concentrated (HHI greater than 1,000, at most 1,800)`
        OTHERWISE                                       JUST `not concentrated (HHI at most 1,000)`

§§ `2.1 helpers for writing a market`

GIVEN name IS A STRING
      share IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Firm in the relevant market`
`a party with a share of` MEANS `Firm in the relevant market` WITH
    `the firm's name` IS name
    `the firm's pre-merger share` IS share
    `the firm is a party to the merger` IS TRUE

GIVEN name IS A STRING
      share IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Firm in the relevant market`
`a rival with a share of` MEANS `Firm in the relevant market` WITH
    `the firm's name` IS name
    `the firm's pre-merger share` IS share
    `the firm is a party to the merger` IS FALSE
